seed.patch -- NETHACK_SEED=<decimal integer> makes a NetHack 3.6.7 game reproducible
(local test builds only; see scripts/README-nethack-local.md).

  * init_random() seeds both RNGs (core + display) from NETHACK_SEED instead
    of /dev/urandom; has_strong_rngseed stays FALSE, so mklev()/goto_level()
    no longer reseed from /dev/urandom on every new/revisited level.
  * Wall-clock inputs to game logic are frozen at 2001-01-01 12:00:00 UTC
    (moon phase 1, not Friday 13th, daytime): phase_of_the_moon(),
    friday_13th(), night(), midnight() and ubirthday (shopkeeper names,
    anthole species, glass gem prices, T-shirt slogans).
  * NETHACK_SEED unset or empty: vanilla behaviour.  Non-integer value: the
    game prints an error and exits before touching the terminal.

Apply from the top of the source tree with: patch -p1 < seed.patch

